    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1344">

                <pb facs="0903" n="787" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg787"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/110.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Alger to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mazatlan</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your instructions of December 18.<anchor n="111" xml:id="d1344-f1"/> Request
                    interpretation as meaning of “all proper protection to property of
                    foreigners.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alger</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1344-f1" n="111" xml:id="d1344-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="frus1913#pg_908">For. Rel. 1913, p. 908</ref>. It reads: “You are
                    instructed to extend all possible and proper protection to the lives and
                    properties of Spanish subjects in your district * * *. This also applies to all
                    other foreign subjects within your district.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
